---
import ToolPage from "../components/ToolPage.astro";
---
<ToolPage
  kind="quotation"
  title="Free Quotation Generator: create a PDF quote online"
  description="Make a clear, professional PDF quotation in your browser. Add your items, a valid-until date and terms, then download it. 2 free quotations every month."
  h1="Free quotation generator"
  lead="Send clients a clear, priced quote before the work starts. Add your items, a valid-until date and your terms, check the live preview, and download a PDF."
  stepsTitle="How to create a quotation in four steps"
  steps={[
    { t: "Add your details.", d: "Your business or name and contact info, so the client knows who the quote is from." },
    { t: "Add the client.", d: "Their name, and an email or address if you want them shown." },
    { t: "Price the work.", d: "One line per deliverable, with a quantity and a rate. Add a discount or tax if they apply." },
    { t: "Set a valid-until date and download.", d: "Add terms such as a deposit, check the preview, then download the PDF and send it." },
  ]}
  includesTitle="What a good quotation includes"
  includes={[
    "Your name or business name and contact details",
    "The client's name",
    "A quotation number and today's date",
    "A valid-until date, so the price doesn't stay open forever",
    "Each deliverable with a clear description, quantity and price",
    "The estimated total, including any tax or discount",
    "Your terms: deposit, payment schedule and what happens if the scope changes",
  ]}
  faqs={[
    { q: "What is the difference between a quotation and an invoice?", a: "A quotation is a priced offer made before the work. An invoice is a request for payment made after the work, or at an agreed milestone. When a client accepts your quote, you use the same figures to make the invoice." },
    { q: "Is a quotation legally binding?", a: "It depends on where you are and how the quote is worded. In many places a quote that the client accepts can form an agreement. For anything important, ask a local professional. This tool does not give legal advice." },
    { q: "How long should a quote stay valid?", a: "Most freelancers use 14 to 30 days. A valid-until date protects you if your costs or availability change." },
    { q: "Is the quotation generator free?", a: "Yes. Create a free account and you get 2 quotations and 2 invoices free every month. The FreelanceDesk app has no limits and can turn an accepted quote into an invoice in one tap." },
    { q: "Is my information uploaded?", a: "No. The quotation is built in your browser, and your form is saved only in this browser. We only store your email and how many free documents you've used." },
  ]}
  related={[
    { href: "/free-invoice-generator/", label: "Free invoice generator" },
    { href: "/blog/how-to-write-a-quotation-that-wins-the-job/", label: "How to write a quotation that wins the job" },
    { href: "/blog/invoice-vs-quotation/", label: "Invoice vs quotation: what's the difference?" },
  ]}
/>
